@participant1 did you try it with the Ingress, like the steps outlined here https://tailscale.com/kb/1236/kubernetes-operator/?q=kubernetes#ingress-resource?

If you do that, you should see that Tailscale operator populates the `status.loadBalancer.ingress.hostname` with a Tailscale FQDN. This will be resolvable in your tailnet like any other Tailscale FQDN and the in-cluster proxy that the Ingress routes to serves HTTPS by default so you don't need to do anything additional to connect to your app in cluster behind the Ingress over HTTPS.

If that does not work, could you paste any errors that you get i.e if `curl` the Ingress hostname and what resources you created?

```
kubectl get ingress nginx -ojsonpath={.status}
{"loadBalancer":{}}
```
